## hydraulic-press

hydraulic-press-ask = How many times does a hydraulic machine gain in force?
hydraulic-press-title = A hydraulic machine of syringes — and a pneumatic one
hydraulic-press-question = Two syringes — a narrow and a wide one — are joined by a tube, all full of water. We measure the pistons’ diameters. We put 2, 4 and 6 weights of 100 g on the wide piston and push the narrow one with the dynamometer until the load starts to rise. Then we push the narrow piston 6 cm down and see how far the wide one rises. At last, if you like, we pour the water out and try the same with air — a pneumatic machine. How many times does such a machine gain in force?
hydraulic-press-plan-optional = 💨 And if we pour the water out and leave air in the syringes — a pneumatic machine? Will it lift the load the same way?
hydraulic-press-plan-optional-2 = 💧 Shall we bring the water back? Fill the syringes with water again — with the same 8 weights.
hydraulic-press-choices = As many times as the wide piston’s area is larger than the narrow one’s
hydraulic-press-choices-2 = As many times as the diameter is larger
hydraulic-press-choices-3 = Not at all — the force is the same
hydraulic-press-setup = Two syringes (5 and 50 mL) joined by a tube, water, 100 g weights, a dynamometer, a ruler
